WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.526
A navigator tells a program manager that five

2
00:00:02.526 --> 00:00:04.803
families this month misread the same renewal letter

3
00:00:04.803 --> 00:00:06.510
and thought their services were ending.

4
00:00:07.180 --> 00:00:10.588
And the easy answer is, that letter uses

5
00:00:10.588 --> 00:00:11.440
required wording.

6
00:00:12.030 --> 00:00:12.610
Some of it might.

7
00:00:12.900 --> 00:00:15.746
But the explanation around it, the headings, a

8
00:00:15.746 --> 00:00:18.593
plain summary at the top, the translations, those

9
00:00:18.593 --> 00:00:19.660
usually can change.

10
00:00:20.090 --> 00:00:22.463
And if the navigator hears, nothing we can

11
00:00:22.463 --> 00:00:23.650
do, they'll stop reporting.

12
00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.180
Feeding back is part of a navigator's job.

13
00:00:26.470 --> 00:00:27.630
Listening is part of ours.

14
00:00:28.360 --> 00:00:30.480
So we rewrite every letter the program sends?

15
00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:31.970
Start smaller.

16
00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:35.295
The Institute for Healthcare Improvement describes the Plan-Do-Study-Act

17
00:00:35.295 --> 00:00:38.109
cycle: plan a test, try it, study what

18
00:00:38.109 --> 00:00:40.220
happened and decide what to change.

19
00:00:40.630 --> 00:00:43.030
Try the new renewal letter with ten families

20
00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:43.930
before ten thousand.

21
00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:46.887
Navigators can tell you quickly whether people understood

22
00:00:46.887 --> 00:00:47.220
it.

23
00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:50.092
Then we can announce that the new letter

24
00:00:50.092 --> 00:00:51.530
cut missed renewals by half.

25
00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:52.720
Careful there.

26
00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:55.095
Measure the step you meant to change, and

27
00:00:55.095 --> 00:00:57.160
say what you compared with and what else

28
00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:58.450
changed at the same time.

29
00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:01.644
There's a real difference between strong evidence and

30
00:01:01.644 --> 00:01:02.380
program-reported results.

31
00:01:03.070 --> 00:01:03.930
What's an example?

32
00:01:04.560 --> 00:01:07.749
The 2021 autism family navigation trial assigned families

33
00:01:07.749 --> 00:01:10.140
by chance, so it's strong evidence.

34
00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:14.039
A newspaper reported that 96 percent of 499

35
00:01:14.039 --> 00:01:17.447
families served by Sacramento County's Cultural Broker program

36
00:01:17.447 --> 00:01:20.430
had emergency referrals closed without court involvement.

37
00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.580
That figure came from the program.

38
00:01:22.930 --> 00:01:25.117
Useful, but there's no comparison group, so it

39
00:01:25.117 --> 00:01:27.030
can't show how much the brokers caused.

40
00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:29.000
And when the fix works?

41
00:01:29.830 --> 00:01:32.127
Give credit to the navigator who spotted it

42
00:01:32.127 --> 00:01:33.850
and the organization they work for.

43
00:01:34.220 --> 00:01:36.040
Tell them what changed, and what couldn't.

44
00:01:36.210 --> 00:01:37.930
That's what keeps the next report coming.

45
00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:42.491
Listen, test small, measure honestly and share the

46
00:01:42.491 --> 00:01:42.980
credit.
